TITLE:: PluginCP
summary:: GUI plugin frame for CuePlayerGUI
categories:: GUI
related:: Classes/CuePlayer, Classes/CuePlayerGUI, Classes/AbstractGUIComponentCP

DESCRIPTION::

PluginCP is the generic frame used by link::Classes/CuePlayerGUI:: for custom GUI plugins supplied through strong::CuePlayer:gui(... options: (plugins: ...))::.

Plugins are GUI-only. They are not registered on the CuePlayer itself; they are configured as part of the GUI options.

SECTION:: Plugin entries

strong::options.plugins:: is a flat array of id/optionsOrPath pairs:

code::[\a, optionsOrPathA, \b, optionsOrPathB]::

strong::optionsOrPath:: is either an Event of plugin options or a String path to a file that evaluates to such an Event.

Relative String paths are resolved relative to the calling file.

If the same plugin id appears more than once, the later entry replaces the earlier one.

SECTION:: Plugin options

DEFINITIONLIST::
## strong::name::
|| Label shown above the frame. Default: code::"Plugin"::.

## strong::height::
|| Height of the content area. Default: code::40::.

## strong::showLabel::
|| Whether to show the label. Default: code::true::.

## strong::build::
|| Function called once when the plugin is created. Receives the PluginCP instance.

## strong::onCue::
|| Function called on CuePlayer dependant updates. Receives code::(plug, cuePlayer, message)::; common messages are code::\current::, code::\next:: and code::\tempo::.

## strong::onCmdPeriod::
|| Function called on CmdPeriod. Receives the PluginCP instance.

## strong::onClear::
|| Function called when the main GUI window closes. Receives the PluginCP instance.
::

All callbacks are optional.

SECTION:: Instance interface

DEFINITIONLIST::
## strong::contentView::
|| A CompositeView bounded to code::280 x options.height::. Place widgets here.

## strong::window::
|| The parent CuePlayerGUI window.

## strong::store(key, value)::
|| Store a value on the plugin instance.

## strong::at(key)::
|| Retrieve a stored value.
::

SECTION:: Example

CODE::
(
a = CuePlayer.new;

a.gui(
	options: (
		plugins: [\basic, "./Plugins/basic.scd"]
	)
);
)
::
